{title: 076 - O Love That Wilt Not Let Me Go}
{artist: Seventh-day Adventist Hymnal}
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: G}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{tag: God the Father}
{tag: }

Verse 1:
[G]O Love that wilt not [Em]let me [G/D]go, [D]I [D7/C]rest my [Bm]weary [G]soul in [D/F#]Thee;
[D7/F#]Igive [G]Thee [Bm/F#]back the life I [Em]owe,
[Em]That [A7]in Thine ocean depths its [D]flow May richer, [G/D]fuller be.

Verse 2:
[G]O Light that [Em]followest [Bm]all [G]my [D/F#]way,
[G]I yield my [Em]flickering [Bm]torch [G]to [D/F#]thee;
[D7/F#]my [G]heart restores [Bm]its borrowed [Em]ray,
[Em]that [A7]in they sunshine's [D7]blaze
[Em]its [A7]day may brighter, [D]fairer [D7]be.

Verse 3:
[G]O Joy that [Em]seekest [D7/C]me [Bm]through [G]pain,
[G]I cannot [Em]close [D]my [D7/C]heart [Bm]to [G]thee;
[D7/F#]I [G]trace the [Bm/F#]rainbow thru the [Em]rain,
[Em]and [A7]feel the promise [D]is [G/D]not [D7]vain,
[Em]that [A7]morn shall [D]tearless [G/D]be.

Verse 4:
[G]O Cross that [Em]liftest [D7/C]up [Bm]my [G]head,
[G]I dare not [Em]ask [D]to [D7/C]fly [Bm]from [G]thee;
[D7/F#]I [G]lay in [Bm/F#]dust life's glory [Em]dead,
[Em]and [A7]from the ground [D]there [G/D]blossoms
[Em]red [A7]life that shall [D]endless [D7]be.
